  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output A.1. Enhanced decent work statistics using innovative sources and statistical standards</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Government of Lesotho, through the Bureau of Statistics, conducted a pilot testing under the ILO pilot study (&#x201c;measuring unpaid domestic and care work&#x201d;).   The objective of the pilot study was to develop and test suitable survey methodology to support countries in the routine and cost-effective production of statistics. The ILO provided technical capacity and financial support through the EU funded Southern Africa Migration Management Project . The ILO provided ongoing assistance to the BOS as per the following :
1) planning and implementation of the validation phase of pilot testing
2) support for the data collection
3) Technical support and training necessary to conduct the work. 
4) Preparation of all pilot materials. 

The ILO participated in the data collection as an observer.

The ILO provided support to Bureau of Statistics to pilot the study which adopted a phased approach to assess the feasibility of regular production of statistics on unpaid domestic and care work via the intermittent integration of a simplified time use (TU) module in national Labour Force Surveys (LFS).

As a key pilot partner country, Lesotho, contributed to the development of the evidence base to inform the ILO&#x2019;s international guidance on best practice for modular TUS and measurement of unpaid domestic and care work via national LFS. 

As a result of the work, ILO has developed the tools, and allied guidance - aligned to the latest international standards on labour statistics and time use measurement. These tools will be used globally.</narrative>
   </description>
